   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law and the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to authorizing the county of Ulster to regulate the registration and licensing of taxicabs, limousines, and livery vehicles",
    "basePrintNo": "S5301",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5301-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §181, Gen Muni L; amd §498, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5301\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law and the vehicle and traffic\nlaw, in relation to authorizing the county of Ulster to regulate the\nregistration and licensing of taxicabs, limousines, and livery vehicles\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill authorizes Ulster County to regulate the registration and\nlicensing of taxicabs, limousines, and livery vehicles.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends subdivision 1 of section 181 of the General Municipal\nLaw to authorize Ulster County to adopt local laws or ordinances regu-\nlating the registration and licensing of taxicabs, limousines and livery\nvehicles.\n\nSection 2: Amends paragraph b of subdivision 1 of section 498 of the\nVehicle and Traffic Law to include Ulster County in the definition of\n\"licensing jurisdiction.\"\n\nSection 3: Effective date\n\nEXISTING LAW:\n\nSimilar legislation has been enacted for Rockland and Suffolk counties\n(Chapters 385 and 382 of 2012).\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis authority has been requested by Ulster County in order to provide\nthe county with the ability to enter into a reciprocity agreement with\nthe New York City Taxi and Limousine Commission to allow livery compa-\nnies which are based in Ulster County to provide service to New York\nCity.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.7448 of 2014 (Similar): Died in Senate Local Government Committee\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
