    "lawCode": "Amd §181, Gen Muni L; amd §498, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5301A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the general municipal law and the\nvehicle and traffic law, in relation to authorizing the county of\nUlster to regulate the registration and licensing of taxicabs,\nlimousines, and livery vehicles\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill authorizes Ulster County to regulate the registration and\nlicensing of taxicabs, limousines, and livery vehicles.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends subdivision 1 of section 181 of the General\nMunicipal Law to authorize Ulster County to adopt local laws or\nordinances regulating the registration and licensing of taxicabs,\nlimousines and livery vehicles.\n\nSection 2: Amends paragraph b of subdivision 1 of section 498 of the\nVehicle and Traffic Law to include Ulster County in the definition of\n\"licensing jurisdiction.\"\n\nSection 3: Effective date\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nSimilar legislation has been enacted for Rockland and Suffolk counties\n(Chapters 385 and 382 of 2012).\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis authority has been requested by Ulster County in order to provide\nthe county with the ability to enter into a reciprocity agreement with\nthe New York City Taxi and Limousine Commission to allow livery\ncompanies which are based in Ulster County to provide service to New\nYork City.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nS.7448 of 2014 (Similar): Died in Senate Local Government Committee\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
